    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence of validations and side-effects applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:109`), which implements the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface.\n\n## Before the controller method runs\n\n1. **Security** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (else 403).\n2. **Deserialization** \u2014 Jackson binds the request body to `OwnerFieldsDto` (note: the DTO, *not* the `Owner` entity, is what gets validated).\n3. **Bean Validation (`@Valid`)** on `OwnerFieldsDto` \u2014 a failure throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, converted to **400** by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/'/-)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (like firstName, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\\\S.*\")` (non-blank)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\\\S.*\")`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` requiring **exactly 10 digits**\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@PastOrPresent` (optional)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n   - **Class-level `@PostcodeValidation`** (custom `ConstraintValidator`) \u2014 if a 4-digit postcode is present, it must fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); unknown cities pass.\n\n## Inside the controller method\n\n4. **Mapping/normalization** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` builds the entity and normalizes:\n   - telephone \u2192 E.164 (`E164.toE164`; can throw `IllegalArgumentException` \u2192 500)\n   - address \u2192 canonical upper-case, whitespace collapsed, `ST/RD/AVE` expanded\n   - email \u2192 lower-cased (via `Owner.setEmail`)\n5. **Disposable-domain block** \u2014 `DisposableDomains.isBlocked` \u2192 **400** if email domain is mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail.\n6. **Load snapshot** \u2014 `clinicService.findAllOwners()` (all subsequent duplicate/cap checks run against this in-memory list, not DB constraints).\n7. **Daily-cap check** \u2014 \u2265100 registrations today \u2192 **429**.\n8. **Per-city cap** \u2014 \u226550 owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409**.\n9. **Set `householdId`** \u2014 SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`, first 12 hex chars.\n10. **Identity-key duplicate** \u2014 exact match of `telephone|email|householdId` against existing owners \u2192 **409**.\n11. **Household duplicate** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold == true`, a matching `householdId` \u2192 **409**.\n12. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 transient flag, true if >80 registrations today.\n13. **Set `namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n14. **Set `customerCode`** \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city, HASH8 = SHA-256 of `telephone + lastName`).\n15. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`, which is the **only `@Transactional` boundary** \u2192 `repository.save`.\n\n## During persist (JPA lifecycle)\n\n16. **`@PrePersist ensureRegistrationDate()`** \u2014 defaults `registrationDate` to today if null, then rolls forward off weekends to a business day.\n17. **`@PostPersist` (`OwnerAuditListener`)** \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line (`owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026`).\n\n## Response\n\n18. Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto` (computes display-only fields: displayName, initials, membership points/level, Luhn check digit, etc. \u2014 no persistence effect).\n19. Return **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n**Notable observations:**\n- The `Owner`/`Person` entity carries its *own* Bean Validation annotations (e.g. `telephone` `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` E.164, `firstName/lastName/address/city` `@NotEmpty`), but these are **not** what `@Valid` checks \u2014 validation is on the DTO. They'd only fire on a validating persistence provider.\n- All uniqueness/cap checks are computed against an in-memory snapshot with no backing DB unique constraint, and there's no transaction spanning the read + save, so they're racy under concurrency.\n- A bad phone number that passes the DTO's \"10 digits\" regex but is rejected by `E164.toE164` surfaces as a **500**, not a 400."
